* Ten-Tec 80282 crystal starting models
*
* The manual documents an eight-pole approximately 9 MHz crystal lattice
* filter and a separate carrier-oscillator crystal, but gives no motional
* parameters or individual crystal frequencies.  These are engineering
* models fitted to the documented carrier-alignment behavior; they are not
* factory crystal specifications.
*
* Pins: 1, 2 = crystal terminals
* Parameters: FS = series resonance, RM = motional loss, CM = motional C,
*             C0 = holder/static capacitance.  LM is derived from FS and CM.
.SUBCKT SSB80282_XTAL 1 2 PARAMS: FS=9.0017MEG RM=22 CM=20F C0=3P
Rmot 1 XM {RM}
Lmot XM XN {1/((6.283185307179586*FS)**2*CM)}
Cmot XN 2 {CM}
Cshunt 1 2 {C0}
.ENDS SSB80282_XTAL

* Separate carrier crystal.  Its fitted motional values let the runner show
* the direction and interaction of C1/C2/C3; absolute frequency still needs
* a measurement from an original crystal.
.SUBCKT SSB80282_BFO_XTAL 1 2 PARAMS: FS=9.0000MEG RM=25 CM=18F C0=3P
Rmot 1 XM {RM}
Lmot XM XN {1/((6.283185307179586*FS)**2*CM)}
Cmot XN 2 {CM}
Cshunt 1 2 {C0}
.ENDS SSB80282_BFO_XTAL
